   5:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c **** /**
   6:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * To use the debugger with a different interface these functions need to be defined
   7:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * This makes it possible to use gdb with various interfaces such as USB, UART, I2C, CAN
   8:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * but possibly also some more exotic ones, maybe debug with local LCD and keypad?
   9:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * */
  10:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c **** 
  11:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c **** 
  12:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c **** /**
  13:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * Sends messages to the debugger 
  14:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * This function should send the characters in the message buffer (7 bit clean).
  15:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * Must be able to handle 512 bytes in the message buffer.
  16:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * Is allowed to block, or rely on DMA/IRQs for non-blocking messages.
  17:./../../firmware/debugger/debugger_port.c ****  * */
